duf is a disk usage/free utility with colorful output, device grouping,
sorting, filtering, inode information, and JSON output.

Building requires google-go-lang (Go 1.23.0 or newer). Dependencies are
provided in a separate vendor archive; compilation does not download
modules or a Go toolchain. Go is not needed to run the built program.

Run "duf" to display mounted filesystems, or "duf /home" to inspect a
specific path. Use "duf --help" for options.

If your shell defines a duf alias (for example, oh-my-zsh), remove it
with "unalias duf" before running the program.
